# Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
artifacts/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
.idea/

# NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# Data that must never reach a repository. Silueta exists to keep people out of corpora; the corpora
# themselves, the rosters they were checked against and the vaults that can undo the work stay local.
*.vault.json
vault.json
roster*.json
*.deid.txt
/data/
/corpus/
/samples/private/
# A real corpus goes in corpus/, which stays ignored however inconvenient that is. The synthetic gold corpus
# that IS committed lives in corpus-synthetic/, named so nobody drops real transcripts beside it by habit.
# (It first went into corpus/ and this rule silently kept it out of two commits, one of which said it was in.)

# …except the made-up ones that document the format.
!**/*.example.json

# The working desk: state, pending work, committee briefs and the audits they produce. Working notes
# name unfinished work and unfixed defects, and none of that is ready for a stranger to read as if it
# were documentation. Public defects become GitHub issues instead — see AI_Tasks/README.md.
AI_Tasks/
.audits/

# Local pack output
out/

# Audio and intermediate files from the corpus generator: regenerable, and large.
tools/corpus/work/
